{
  "VghLantern__GlazeBarSystem__Meta": {
    "SchemaVersion": "2.0.0",
    "CreatedDate": "05-Aug-2026",
    "Description": "The Vale roof glaze bar as built: a cap, a core and a trim sharing one section datum. Cap and core are fixed; only the trim depth is configurable.",
    "SectionFrameNote": "All parts are authored in one shared section frame taken from Na__Asset__Plan2D__Top. Section +x runs across the bar, section +y runs out through the roof, and section 0,0 is the glaze bar datum. The parts assemble with no fitting and their solid areas do not overlap.",
    "ElementTypeVocabulary": [
      "Structural",
      "Trim",
      "By Others",
      "Flashing",
      "Glazing"
    ],
    "OverallWidthMm": 40.584,
    "OverallWidthNote": "The widest point across the assembled bar, which is the cap. Consumed by the 2D profile trace overlay, where a bar is drawn as a band of its real width.",
    "HandAuthored": true,
    "HandAuthoredNote": "Written by hand rather than generated. This is a fixed three part system, not a catalogue: a build utility scanning a folder could not know which asset fills which slot.",
    "AssetResolutionNote": "Parts name an AssetId and nothing else. The file behind an id is resolved through VghLantern__AssetRegistry__.json, which is the one place a path is written down. This index carried a LibraryRoot and a JsonUrl per part until 21-Aug-2026, when the folder was renamed 45_1000__GlazeBars to 45_2000__GlazeBars__Profiles and every one of them pointed at a file that no longer existed, with nothing to report it.",
    "ProductCodeNote": "Renumbered 45_10xx to 45_20xx on 21-Aug-2026. The x_1xxx block is the component library and the x_2xxx block is the profile library, matching the ridge and hip systems, so a code now says which library holds it. TrimOptionId is a product code and moved with them; ProjectSchemaValidator migrates the stored value on load."
  },
